## 11. Evaluation and Back-Test Protocol

### 11.1 Objectives

Prove (a) shortlist captures real cases, (b) LLM confirmation adds precision vs price-only, (c) narrative saves analyst time, without leakage.

### 11.2 Datasets

* **Positives:** 3 frozen cases + expand to 10-20 AMF/SEC enforcement TAME/insider cases on equities with known event dates (collect from AMF sanctions, SEC litigation releases — Rutgers deep-learning study uses litigation releases + market + social data).
* **Negatives:** (i) top exposure-break stocks with no price-moving news in window (benign rebalancing), (ii) large price jumps with no exposure break (macro/sector), (iii) random stocks. Needed to estimate false-positive rate.
* **As-of reconstruction:** internal files as stored at D (no restatement), market data vintage, news snapshot with `pubDate <= D-1` (Common Crawl / GDELT / licensed archive, not live search).

### 11.3 Metrics

* Stage 2: recall@50 (positives in S1), mean rank, false-shortlist rate.
* Stage 3: precision/recall of event confirmation vs expert labels (LSEG 9-point protocol, 2 annotators + adjudication), citation faithfulness (% claims with valid quote/URL).
* End-to-end: precision@k (k=10,20), recall, F1, analyst time per alert (A/B vs manual), override/agreement rate, STOR conversion rate (long-term).
* Robustness: ablation without LLM (price+exposure only), without exposure (price+news à la LSEG), small vs large LLM, zero vs few-shot, with/without market adjustment.
* Statistics: Mann-Whitney for configuration gains, AUC for graded scores (Nordgren), Boehmer/Corrado for market abnormality significance.

### 11.4 Leakage controls

* Record LLM knowledge cutoff; run RAG-only (no parametric) vs parametric-only ablation; test with model cutoff < event date; forbid web browsing beyond dated snapshot in back-test; document retrieval timestamps.

### 11.5 Analyst study

* 2-3 IMAD analysts label 110-article sample (LSEG replication) + 30 alerts. Measure inter-rater kappa, time saved, usefulness 1-5, trust. Few-shot examples drawn from this set.

### 11.6 Acceptance for POC success (proposal)

* ≥2/3 frozen cases in S1 and S2 with correct event date ±1bd and direction-consistent narrative.
* Precision@20 ≥ price-only baseline +15pp or triage time -30% with no recall loss.
* Zero hallucinations with fake URL in sample (100% citation validity).
* Documented limitations + v1.1 plan. No production deployment gate yet.

